Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese Easy Chat keyboard
Applies after 0005-port-hooks.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese ROM's Easy Chat keyboard: the alphabet mode picks words by kana row
(あ to わ and そのた, the others) from all 45 gEasyChatWordsByLetterPointers lists,
which tools/localize_japanese.py stages in the ROM's kana order with the keyboard's
rows of text (gText_EasyChatKeyboard_*). Group names and words are in three
columns, at the ROM's positions, and the rectangle cursor is one sprite of the
Japanese graphics. The main screen is the Japanese one too: phrases of three words
a row (3x2 and 3x3 instead of 2x3 and 2x5) in the ROM's frames, the words run on a
tile a character, the title, messages and cursor sit where the ROM puts them, and
the footer's labels are in the window graphics. Staging puts the cursor and window
graphics only into a tree with this patch (it looks for EASY_CHAT_KANA_KEYBOARD).

